.TH CTX 1 "2026-07-25" "ctx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctx \- share Claude Code and Codex context over a Tailscale tailnet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctx
.br
.B ctx tui
.br
.B ctx host
[\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-source\fR \fISESSION.jsonl\fR]
.br
.B ctx host ls
[\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B ctx ls
[\fIHOST\fR]
.br
.B ctx tail
[\fB\-f\fR] [\fIHOST/FEED\fR]
.br
.B ctx continue
[\fB\-\-with\fR \fIclaude|codex\fR] [\fIHOST/FEED\fR]
.br
.B ctx doctor
.br
.B ctx update
.br
.B ctx completion
\fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctx
publishes normalized, read-only agent context from a producer and lets
consumers discover, inspect, tail, or continue it over a private Tailscale
tailnet.
.PP
When standard input and output are interactive terminals, bare
.B ctx
opens the context dashboard. In scripts, CI, and redirected pipelines it
prints command help instead. Explicit subcommands never change their output
format based on the dashboard.
.SH DASHBOARD
.B ctx tui
opens the dashboard explicitly. It discovers local Claude Code and Codex
sessions alongside shared contexts reachable over the tailnet. Local and
remote inventories load independently.
.PP
Resting on a row loads a session peek containing the latest user request,
activity counts, recent tool names, and up to four recent human and agent
turns. This summary is deterministic and extractive. It runs in process over
normalized events with display redaction and does not call a local or cloud
LLM. Local previews stream from the selected session file into fixed-size
summary state. Shared previews fetch a size-limited digest from the selected
provider.
.PP
Press
.B v
to replace the dashboard with a full-screen transcript inspector. Page 1
contains the newest history. Each page uses the available terminal height,
with one chronological entry per row. Use PageUp or
.B [
for older pages, PageDown or
.B ]
for newer pages, and Home or End to jump to the oldest or newest page. Escape
returns to the dashboard. Resizing retains approximately the same position in
history. Tool entries expose the tool name and result boundary but not raw
tool arguments or output.
.PP
Preview reads are debounced, cached by the session's content version, and
cancelled when the selection changes. The local scope defaults to the current
workspace. The layout is side by side at 100 columns or wider, stacked below
100 columns, and requires at least a 60 by 18 terminal.
.PP
The dashboard opens with a roughly two-second dog-and-cat string-phone
animation. Press any key to skip it.
.SS Keys
.TP
.B Tab, Shift\-Tab
Change the focused panel.
.TP
.B Up, Down, j, k
Move the selection.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move five rows.
.TP
.B v
Open the selected session's full-screen transcript. Inside the transcript,
PageUp, PageDown, [, ], Home, and End navigate pages; Escape returns to the
dashboard.
.TP
.B /
Filter the focused panel.
.TP
.B a
Toggle current-workspace and all-workspaces local discovery.
.TP
.B r
Refresh status, both inventories, and the selected preview.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the actions available for the selected item.
.TP
.B h
Host the selected local session.
.TP
.B t, f
Tail the selected shared context once, or follow new revisions.
.TP
.B c
Continue the selected shared context with an installed agent.
.TP
.B ?
Open or close keyboard help.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.PP
Selecting an action closes the alternate screen before starting the existing
.BR host ,
.BR tail ,
or
.B continue
flow.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTX_NO_ANIMATION
When non-empty, disable motion in the dashboard and standalone installer. The
installer still prints the final static welcome with installation metadata on
the first install.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Open the interactive context dashboard. This command requires a terminal.
.TP
.B host
Publish the current or explicitly selected local agent session. The process
stays in the foreground until interrupted.
.TP
.B host ls
List hostable Claude Code and Codex sessions. The default scope is the current
workspace; use
.B \-\-all
to scan every local workspace or
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B ls
List feeds from one host, or discover feeds from online tailnet peers when no
host is given.
.TP
.B tail
Print the latest neutral digest. Use
.B \-f
or
.B \-\-follow
to poll for new revisions.
.TP
.B continue
Fetch and pin a neutral digest, then start Claude Code or Codex with that
digest as quarantined context. This does not import a native session.
.TP
.B doctor
Check installation, Tailscale connectivity, local agent commands, and session
discovery.
.TP
.B update
Update using the installation method recorded for the current binary.
.TP
.B completion
Write shell completion setup for Bash, Zsh, or Fish.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the dashboard:
.PP
.EX
ctx
ctx tui
.EE
.PP
Host a selected local session:
.PP
.EX
ctx host ls
ctx host \-\-source ~/.claude/projects/.../session.jsonl
.EE
.PP
Consume a shared context:
.PP
.EX
ctx ls
ctx tail \-f ctx://dev\-laptop/payments
ctx continue ctx://dev\-laptop/payments \-\-with codex
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success or user cancellation and non-zero for invalid arguments,
missing prerequisites, discovery failures, or command execution errors.
.SH SECURITY
The provider exposes normalized, read-only history rather than native session
files. Remote content is quarantined and cannot supply executable host code.
Tailscale Serve provides transport identity and tailnet access policy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/delightroom/ctx
Project documentation
.UE
